                <pb facs="0900" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg780"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/834: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schurman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-19T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19, 1922—1
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>177. Your 299 July 10, 7 p.m. has been copied to the American Group for comment.
                    You will be informed of its reply. For your confidential information you are
                    advised that the Department does not anticipate a favorable reply. Is the
                    Department to understand that proposal outlined in your 299, if adopted, takes
                    the place of postponement of indemnity payments proposed in your 280, June 23, 9
                        a.m.?<anchor n="37" xml:id="d568-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
